  "questions": [
    {
      "boundary": "The broker boundary between Redpanda and Apache Kafka. After the move, Catalog Management (catalog service and image service) produces and consumes on Kafka; every other service (tenant, product-query, category-query) stays on Redpanda. Traffic crosses the boundary in two places. tenant.tenant.events is produced on Redpanda by the tenant service and consumed by both moved services (inbound). catalog.product.events, catalog.category.events and catalog.attribute.events are produced on Kafka by the moved services and consumed by the query services on Redpanda (outbound). The image service's consumption of catalog.product.events stays inside the boundary, because both producers of that topic (catalog and image service) move.",
      "boundary_named": true,
      "id": "Q1",
      "services": [
        "ecommerce-catalog-service",
        "ecommerce-image-service"
      ],
      "verdict": "MATCHED"
